IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa14-nouns`
IMPORT `coa14-ch10-reduction`
IMPORT `coa-proc-capital-reduction`

-- coa-proc-capital-reduction-tests.l4: tests for coa-proc-capital-reduction.l4 (Companies Act 2006, ss 641 to 653).
-- Every expected outcome is written from the text of the section named beside it, before the run, and never copied from the output.
-- A #TRACE prints FULFILLED, a BREACH or a still-open obligation (RESIDUAL) and no assertion line, so the expected outcome sits on the
-- `-- EXPECT` line directly above each trace and is read against the Result block by expect_check.py.
-- The traces count calendar days. For ss 642(1)(a) day 0 is the day the directors make the solvency statement; for ss 644(1) and (5) it is the
-- day the resolution is passed; for s 646(3)(b) it is the day the court publishes the notice.

§ `Tests for the capital reduction procedure`

§§ `Fixtures: the facts of route one (the six fields, in order)`

-- the fields, in order: the company is a private company limited by shares; the resolution is a special resolution; the statement is made in
-- accordance with s 643; after the reduction no member would hold shares other than redeemable shares; the date of the statement; the date of the resolution.
`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution` MEANS `ss 641-653 route one facts` OF TRUE, (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), FALSE, (Date 1 3 2026), (Date 11 3 2026)
`facts: a statement made 15 days before the resolution` MEANS `ss 641-653 route one facts` OF TRUE, (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), FALSE, (Date 1 3 2026), (Date 16 3 2026)
`facts: a statement made 16 days before the resolution` MEANS `ss 641-653 route one facts` OF TRUE, (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), FALSE, (Date 1 3 2026), (Date 17 3 2026)
`facts: a statement dated after the resolution` MEANS `ss 641-653 route one facts` OF TRUE, (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), FALSE, (Date 12 3 2026), (Date 11 3 2026)
`facts: a public company` MEANS `ss 641-653 route one facts` OF FALSE, (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), FALSE, (Date 1 3 2026), (Date 11 3 2026)
`facts: a statement not made in accordance with section 643` MEANS `ss 641-653 route one facts` OF TRUE, (JUST TRUE), (JUST FALSE), FALSE, (Date 1 3 2026), (Date 11 3 2026)
`facts: a reduction that would leave no member holding other than redeemable shares` MEANS `ss 641-653 route one facts` OF TRUE, (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), TRUE, (Date 1 3 2026), (Date 11 3 2026)
`facts: no special resolution` MEANS `ss 641-653 route one facts` OF TRUE, (JUST FALSE), (JUST TRUE), FALSE, (Date 1 3 2026), (Date 11 3 2026)

-- the creditors: consent, discharged, determined, secured.
`a creditor who consented` MEANS `s 648(2) creditor entitled to object` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a creditor whose claim was secured` MEANS `s 648(2) creditor entitled to object` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a creditor who has neither consented nor been satisfied` MEANS `s 648(2) creditor entitled to object` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`creditors who are all satisfied` MEANS LIST `a creditor who consented`, `a creditor whose claim was secured`
`creditors of whom one is not satisfied` MEANS LIST `a creditor who consented`, `a creditor who has neither consented nor been satisfied`

§§ `Assertions: the gates this module adds`

-- s 641(1)(a), (2): a private company limited by shares with a statement made in accordance with s 643 may use route one.
#ASSERT `ss 641-653 route one is open to the company` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`)
-- s 641(1)(a): a public company is not within route one.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 641-653 route one is open to the company` (`facts: a public company`)))
-- s 642(1)(a): a statement not made in accordance with s 643 does not support the resolution.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 641-653 route one is open to the company` (`facts: a statement not made in accordance with section 643`)))
-- s 641(2): route one is not open where no member would be left holding shares other than redeemable shares.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 641-653 route one is open to the company` (`facts: a reduction that would leave no member holding other than redeemable shares`)))
-- s 642(1)(a): a statement made 10 days before the resolution is in time.
#ASSERT `ss 641-653 the resolution was passed within 15 days after the solvency statement` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`)
-- s 642(1)(a): "not more than 15 days before": 15 days before is in time.
#ASSERT `ss 641-653 the resolution was passed within 15 days after the solvency statement` (`facts: a statement made 15 days before the resolution`)
-- s 642(1)(a): 16 days before is out of time.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 641-653 the resolution was passed within 15 days after the solvency statement` (`facts: a statement made 16 days before the resolution`)))
-- s 642(1)(a): a statement dated after the resolution is not "before" it.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 641-653 the resolution was passed within 15 days after the solvency statement` (`facts: a statement dated after the resolution`)))
-- s 644(1): the deliveries are owed on route one with a special resolution and a statement in time.
#ASSERT `ss 641-653 the deliveries of s 644 are owed` (`facts: a statement made 15 days before the resolution`)
-- s 644(1): no deliveries are owed where the statement was 16 days before the resolution.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 641-653 the deliveries of s 644 are owed` (`facts: a statement made 16 days before the resolution`)))
-- s 644(1): no deliveries are owed where the resolution is not a special resolution.
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 641-653 the deliveries of s 644 are owed` (`facts: no special resolution`)))

§§ `Traces: s 642(1)(a), the 15 days between the solvency statement and the resolution`

-- s 642(1)(a): the resolution is passed on day 10, in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 642(1)(a) the company's power to pass the resolution within 15 days of the solvency statement` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 642(1)(a) the company passes the special resolution for reducing share capital` AT 10

-- s 642(1)(a): the resolution is passed on day 15, the last day.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 642(1)(a) the company's power to pass the resolution within 15 days of the solvency statement` (`facts: a statement made 15 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 642(1)(a) the company passes the special resolution for reducing share capital` AT 15

-- s 642(1)(a): the resolution is passed on day 16, more than 15 days after the statement, so the statement does not support it.
-- EXPECT changed after independent review: a resolution on day 16 closes the route and is no breach, because s 642(1)(a) defines when a resolution is supported by a statement and puts no duty on the company (src:8553-8554)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 642(1)(a) the company's power to pass the resolution within 15 days of the solvency statement` (`facts: a statement made 16 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 642(1)(a) the company passes the special resolution for reducing share capital` AT 16

-- s 642(1)(a): no resolution is passed and the 15 days run out.
-- EXPECT changed after independent review: a company that passes no resolution within the 15 days has lost the use of the statement and is in no breach (src:8553-8554)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 642(1)(a) the company's power to pass the resolution within 15 days of the solvency statement` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

-- s 641(1)(a): a public company has no route one, so no window runs.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 642(1)(a) the company's power to pass the resolution within 15 days of the solvency statement` (`facts: a public company`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

§§ `Traces: s 644(1), the copy of the solvency statement and the statement of capital`

-- s 644(1): delivered on day 7, in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 644(1) the company's duty to deliver the solvency statement and the statement of capital, as a procedure` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 644(1) the company delivers to the registrar a copy of the solvency statement and a statement of capital` AT 7

-- s 644(1): delivered on day 15, the last day ("Within 15 days after the resolution").
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 644(1) the company's duty to deliver the solvency statement and the statement of capital, as a procedure` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 644(1) the company delivers to the registrar a copy of the solvency statement and a statement of capital` AT 15

-- s 644(1): delivered on day 16, one day late.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 644(1) the company's duty to deliver the solvency statement and the statement of capital, as a procedure` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 644(1) the company delivers to the registrar a copy of the solvency statement and a statement of capital` AT 16

-- s 644(1): nothing is delivered and the 15 days run out.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 644(1) the company's duty to deliver the solvency statement and the statement of capital, as a procedure` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 16)

-- s 642(1)(a): the statement was made 16 days before the resolution, so route one's support fails and no delivery is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 644(1) the company's duty to deliver the solvency statement and the statement of capital, as a procedure` (`facts: a statement made 16 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

§§ `Traces: s 644(5), the directors' statement`

-- s 644(5): delivered on day 15, the last day ("within 15 days after the resolution is passed").
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 644(5) the company's duty to deliver the directors' statement, as a procedure` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 644(5) the company delivers to the registrar a statement by the directors confirming that the solvency statement was made in time and provided to members` AT 15

-- s 644(5): delivered on day 16, one day late.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 644(5) the company's duty to deliver the directors' statement, as a procedure` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 644(5) the company delivers to the registrar a statement by the directors confirming that the solvency statement was made in time and provided to members` AT 16

-- s 641(1)(a): there is no special resolution, so no directors' statement is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 644(5) the company's duty to deliver the directors' statement, as a procedure` (`facts: no special resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

§§ `Traces: s 644(1) and (5) together`

-- s 644(1) and (5): both deliveries made in time, the second on the last day.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 644 the company's two deliveries to the registrar` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 644(1) the company delivers to the registrar a copy of the solvency statement and a statement of capital` AT 3
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 644(5) the company delivers to the registrar a statement by the directors confirming that the solvency statement was made in time and provided to members` AT 15

-- s 644(1) and (5): the copy and the statement of capital are in time; the directors' statement is delivered on day 16.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 644 the company's two deliveries to the registrar` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 644(1) the company delivers to the registrar a copy of the solvency statement and a statement of capital` AT 3
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 644(5) the company delivers to the registrar a statement by the directors confirming that the solvency statement was made in time and provided to members` AT 16

-- s 644(1) and (5): neither is delivered and the 15 days run out.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 644 the company's two deliveries to the registrar` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 16)

§§ `Traces: s 644(3), the registrar registers on receipt`

-- s 644(3): the documents are received and registered on day 2.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 644(3) the registrar's duty to register the documents, as a procedure` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the registrar` DOES `s 644(3) the registrar registers the documents delivered to him` AT 2

-- s 644(3): the documents are received and by day 30 nothing is registered; the Act gives no later limit, so the duty stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 644(3) the registrar's duty to register the documents, as a procedure` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 644(3): the documents have not been received, so there is nothing to register.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 644(3) the registrar's duty to register the documents, as a procedure` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§§ `Traces: the offences of route one (ss 643(4), 644(7), 644(8))`

-- s 643(4): a director in default makes a solvency statement without reasonable grounds and it is delivered.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 643(4) the director's duty not to deliver a solvency statement made without reasonable grounds` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 a director of the company who is in default` DOES `s 643(4) a director makes a solvency statement without reasonable grounds and the statement is delivered to the registrar` AT 5

-- s 643(4): nothing of the kind has happened; the prohibition stays open, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 643(4) the director's duty not to deliver a solvency statement made without reasonable grounds` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 643(4): "every director who is in default": a director who is not in default commits no offence.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 643(4) the director's duty not to deliver a solvency statement made without reasonable grounds` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 a director of the company who is in default` DOES `s 643(4) a director makes a solvency statement without reasonable grounds and the statement is delivered to the registrar` AT 5

-- s 644(7): the company delivers a solvency statement not provided to members, and the officer is in default.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 644(7) the officer's duty not to let the company deliver a solvency statement that was not provided to members` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 an officer of the company who is in default` DOES `s 644(7) the company delivers to the registrar a solvency statement that was not provided to members` AT 3

-- s 644(7): an officer who is not in default commits no offence.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 644(7) the officer's duty not to let the company deliver a solvency statement that was not provided to members` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 an officer of the company who is in default` DOES `s 644(7) the company delivers to the registrar a solvency statement that was not provided to members` AT 3

-- s 644(8)(b): default is made in complying with s 644 and the officer is in default.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 644(8)(b) the officer's duty not to be in default in complying with section 644` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 an officer of the company who is in default` DOES `s 644(8) the officer is in default in the company's default in complying with section 644` AT 20

-- s 644(8)(b): an officer who is not in default commits no offence.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 644(8)(b) the officer's duty not to be in default in complying with section 644` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 an officer of the company who is in default` DOES `s 644(8) the officer is in default in the company's default in complying with section 644` AT 20

§§ `Traces: route two, the application to the court (s 645) and the list of creditors (s 646)`

-- s 645(1): the company has passed a resolution and applies on day 12; the power has no time limit.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 645(1) the company's power to apply to the court for an order confirming the reduction` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 645(1) the company applies to the court for an order confirming the reduction` AT 12

-- s 645(1): the company has not applied by day 40; the power stays open, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 645(1) the company's power to apply to the court for an order confirming the reduction` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

-- s 645(1): "Where a company has passed a resolution": none has been passed, so the power does not arise.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 645(1) the company's power to apply to the court for an order confirming the reduction` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

-- s 646(2): section 646 applies and the court settles the list on day 20.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 646(2) the court's duty to settle a list of creditors entitled to object` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the court` DOES `s 646(2) the court settles a list of creditors entitled to object` AT 20

-- s 646(2): section 646 applies and by day 60 no list is settled; the Act gives the court no time, so the duty stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 646(2) the court's duty to settle a list of creditors entitled to object` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 646(1): "Where this section applies": the court has directed that it does not, so there is no list to settle.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 646(2) the court's duty to settle a list of creditors entitled to object` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 646(3)(b): the notice is published on 15 January 2026 and fixes 15 March 2026, 59 days later; the creditor claims on day 59.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 646(3)(b) the creditor's power to claim to be entered on the list by the day fixed` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 a creditor not entered on the list` DOES `s 646(3)(b) a creditor not entered on the list claims to be entered` AT 59

-- s 646(3)(b): the creditor claims on day 60, a day after the day fixed.
-- EXPECT changed after independent review: a creditor who claims after the day fixed is excluded from the right of objecting and has done no wrong (src:8621)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 646(3)(b) the creditor's power to claim to be entered on the list by the day fixed` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 a creditor not entered on the list` DOES `s 646(3)(b) a creditor not entered on the list claims to be entered` AT 60

-- s 646(3)(b): the creditor does nothing and the day fixed passes.
-- EXPECT changed after independent review: a creditor who does not claim is excluded from the right of objecting and has done no wrong (src:8621)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 646(3)(b) the creditor's power to claim to be entered on the list by the day fixed` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

-- s 646(3)(b): "creditors not entered on the list": this creditor is on the list, so no claim is needed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 646(3)(b) the creditor's power to claim to be entered on the list by the day fixed` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 60)

§§ `Traces: s 647(1), the offences in connection with the list of creditors`

-- s 647(1)(a)(i): an officer intentionally or recklessly conceals the name of a creditor entitled to object.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 647(1) the officer's duty not to conceal or misrepresent a creditor's name, debt or claim` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 an officer of the company` DOES `s 647(1)(a)(i) an officer intentionally or recklessly conceals the name of a creditor entitled to object` AT 10

-- s 647(1)(a)(ii): an officer misrepresents the nature or amount of a creditor's debt or claim.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 647(1) the officer's duty not to conceal or misrepresent a creditor's name, debt or claim` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 an officer of the company` DOES `s 647(1)(a)(ii) an officer intentionally or recklessly misrepresents the nature or amount of a creditor's debt or claim` AT 10

-- s 647(1)(b): an officer is knowingly concerned in such a concealment or misrepresentation.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 647(1) the officer's duty not to conceal or misrepresent a creditor's name, debt or claim` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 an officer of the company` DOES `s 647(1)(b) an officer is knowingly concerned in such a concealment or misrepresentation` AT 10

-- s 647(1): nothing of the kind has happened; the three prohibitions stay open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 647(1) the officer's duty not to conceal or misrepresent a creditor's name, debt or claim` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

-- s 647(1): the person is not an officer of the company (s 1173(1)), so commits no offence.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 647(1) the officer's duty not to conceal or misrepresent a creditor's name, debt or claim` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 an officer of the company` DOES `s 647(1)(a)(i) an officer intentionally or recklessly conceals the name of a creditor entitled to object` AT 10

§§ `Traces: s 648, the court's order`

-- s 648(2): one creditor entitled to object has neither consented nor been satisfied, and the court confirms the reduction on day 5.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 648(2) the court's duty not to confirm the reduction unless satisfied about every creditor entitled to object` (`creditors of whom one is not satisfied`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the court` DOES `s 648(1) the court makes an order confirming the reduction` AT 5

-- s 648(2): every creditor entitled to object has consented or been secured, and the court confirms on day 5.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 648(2) the court's duty not to confirm the reduction unless satisfied about every creditor entitled to object` (`creditors who are all satisfied`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the court` DOES `s 648(1) the court makes an order confirming the reduction` AT 5

-- s 648(2): one creditor is not satisfied and the court has not confirmed; the prohibition stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 648(2) the court's duty not to confirm the reduction unless satisfied about every creditor entitled to object` (`creditors of whom one is not satisfied`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 648(1): every creditor is satisfied and the court makes the order on day 5; the power has no time limit.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 648(1) the court's power to make an order confirming the reduction` (`creditors who are all satisfied`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the court` DOES `s 648(1) the court makes an order confirming the reduction` AT 5

-- s 648(2): one creditor is not satisfied, so the power of s 648(1) is not encoded as open.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 648(1) the court's power to make an order confirming the reduction` (`creditors of whom one is not satisfied`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 649, the registration of the order and the certificate`

-- s 649(1) and (5): the order and statement are delivered, registered on day 3 and certified on day 4.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 649(1) the registrar's duty to register the order and the statement of capital, and then to certify the registration` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the registrar` DOES `s 649(1) the registrar registers the order and the statement of capital` AT 3
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the registrar` DOES `s 649(5) the registrar certifies the registration` AT 4

-- s 649(5): registered on day 3 and by day 10 not yet certified; the Act gives no time, so the certificate stays owed.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 649(1) the registrar's duty to register the order and the statement of capital, and then to certify the registration` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the registrar` DOES `s 649(1) the registrar registers the order and the statement of capital` AT 3
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 649(1): delivered and not yet registered by day 10; the duty stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 649(1) the registrar's duty to register the order and the statement of capital, and then to certify the registration` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 650(2): the registrar is barred from registering the order, so the duty of s 649(1) is not owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 649(1) the registrar's duty to register the order and the statement of capital, and then to certify the registration` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 649(1): the statement of capital has not been delivered, so the registrar has nothing to register.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 649(1) the registrar's duty to register the order and the statement of capital, and then to certify the registration` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

§§ `Traces added: s 646(1), and the in-time and gate cases of s 644(5), s 644 and s 646(3)(b)`

-- s 646(1): section 646 applies, the creditor has an admissible debt and shows a real likelihood; the creditor objects on day 10 (the power has no time limit).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 646(1) the creditor's power to object to the reduction of capital` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 a creditor entitled to object` DOES `s 646(1) the creditor objects to the reduction of capital` AT 10

-- s 646(1): the creditor is entitled and has not objected by day 40; the power stays open, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 646(1) the creditor's power to object to the reduction of capital` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

-- s 646(1)(b): the creditor cannot show a real likelihood that the reduction would leave the company unable to discharge the debt, so is not entitled to object.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 646(1) the creditor's power to object to the reduction of capital` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

-- s 644(5): the directors' statement is delivered on day 7, in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 644(5) the company's duty to deliver the directors' statement, as a procedure` (`facts: a statement made 10 days before the resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 the company` DOES `s 644(5) the company delivers to the registrar a statement by the directors confirming that the solvency statement was made in time and provided to members` AT 7

-- s 644(1) and (5): there is no special resolution, so neither delivery is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 644 the company's two deliveries to the registrar` (`facts: no special resolution`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

-- s 646(3)(b): the creditor claims on day 30, well before the day fixed (day 59).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 646(3)(b) the creditor's power to claim to be entered on the list by the day fixed` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 641-653 a creditor not entered on the list` DOES `s 646(3)(b) a creditor not entered on the list claims to be entered` AT 30


-- READS-DIFFERENTLY-ON-MAIN:
